{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport pymupdf\npdf=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor index in [7,8]:\n print('\\\\nPAGE',index+1,'\\\\n',pdf[index].get_text(clip=pymupdf.Rect(105,65,507,750),sort=True))\n pdf[index].get_pixmap(matrix=pymupdf.Matrix(1.1,1.1)).save('/tmp/current-page-'+str(index+1)+'.png')\nPY\nrg 'Overfull|undefined|Warning' paper.log | tail -7\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport pymupdf\npdf=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\nfor index in [7,8]:\n print('\\\\nPAGE',index+1,'\\\\n',pdf[index].get_text(clip=pymupdf.Rect(105,65,507,750),sort=True))\n pdf[index].get_pixmap(matrix=pymupdf.Matrix(1.1,1.1)).save('/tmp/current-page-'+str(index+1)+'.png')\nPY\nrg 'Overfull|undefined|Warning' paper.log | tail -7\"","aggregated_output":"\nPAGE 8 \n                             Score control     PPI++      PPI     Exact binomial\n\n\n                    (a) C5 width distribution                              (b) Collapse counts\n             1.0\n                                                      Score control  0\n              CDF\n                                                     PPI++                  115\n             0.5\n                                                                       PPI  2                                          Empirical                                                     Exact binomial  0\n             0.0\n               0.000  0.025  0.050  0.075  0.100                 0      50     100\n                              Interval width                             Zero-width intervals                 Scienti\n\n          Figure 3: C5 rare-outcome diagnostic, using all 256 endpoint records. (a) Empirical CDFs retain\n           the mass at zero on a linear width axis. (b) Collapsed-interval counts. Labeled normal inference,\n          omitted from this four-method display, also has 115 zero-width intervals. The associated coverage\n           values appear in Table 1. Avoiding collapse does not establish nominal coverage or superiority to\n           exact-binomial inference.\n\n\n\n               It cannot establish that splines caused the gain or that cross-fitting improved width. The unavailable\n           controlled comparisons are missing evidence, not measured negative results.\n\n\n         Sampling and source provenance restrict interpretation.  The iid common-population assump-\n            tions are central to both correction and the safety argument. The archive does not identify whether           Agentic\n          each generator satisfies them, whether sampling masks are independent, or whether population truths\n         were constructed analytically or from a finite external pool. We retain the stipulated population target\n         and recorded truths, while avoiding a stronger certification of the sampling design. Likewise, source\n          hashes preserve provenance, but readable method-family alignment does not establish byte-level\n            identity with the sealed executable. This limits attribution without erasing the recorded endpoint\n          comparison.     The\n          Reproducibility is partial, not end-to-end.  The included extraction script reproduces the numer-\n             ical tables, plotted uncertainty, and width distributions from the read-only evidence registry. It does\n           not recreate the unknown generators or rerun the original evaluation. The source archive and seeds\n         document what is available, but missing n, N, data versions, and final implementation snapshot\n           prevent an honest claim of full experimental reproducibility. There are no measured named-dataset   by\n             results, verified transfer results, or robustness analyses beyond the recorded conditions. These omis-\n           sions materially limit external validity.\n\n\n           Practical interpretation.  For fixed-input comparisons, assess coverage before interpreting width.\n           Paired differences remain meaningful when comparator widths vanish, and exact inference supplies\n          an important boundary reference. Selecting an interval after observing its realized width requires its\n        own coverage argument. Here, these principles reveal a modest local gain and substantial comparator\n          dependence, not a generally preferable interval. They motivate controlled follow-up rather than a\n          deployment recommendation.\n\n\n        7  CONCLUSION\n\n          Frozen labels, unlabeled observations, and predictions do not mathematically eliminate all room foreneratedmore efficient mean inference. A score-only control can exploit a better approximation to the con-\n            ditional outcome mean; the fixed-control variance identity specifies this opportunity and the infor-\n          mation it cannot recover. Whether a fitted procedure converts that opportunity into valid, narrower\n            intervals is a separate empirical and theoretical question.\n\nPAGE 9 \n          The paired records provide a bounded answer. Score control is slightly narrower than evaluated\n         PPI++ in C2, but wider in the other six conditions. In the low-prevalence condition it avoids ob-\n           served collapsed intervals and has much higher coverage than two asymptotic comparators, yet its\n          width advantage over exact-binomial inference is unresolved and nominal validity remains unestab-\n            lished. Missing calibration ablations prevent a component-level interpretation, and missing genera-\n            tion metadata prevent reconstruction of the complete study. The defensible conclusion is therefore\n            condition-specific: inference-side flexibility may change width, but this evidence does not establish\n          a uniformly shorter, statistically valid replacement for existing intervals under fixed inputs.                 Scienti\n           Agentic\n     The\n   by\nenerated\nPackage epstopdf Warning: Shell escape feature is not enabled.\nLaTeX Warning: Label(s) may have changed. Rerun to get cross-references right.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
